✅ Two Pointer Pattern — Before You Start Checklist
Ask yourself these 5 questions in order:

1️⃣ Is the data sorted (or can be sorted)?

    ✔️ Sorted array / string
    ✔️ Monotonic order (increasing / decreasing)

    ✅ YES → Two pointers is possible
    ❌ NO → Two pointers usually NOT valid

    Example:
        [1, 2, 4, 7, 11] ✅
        [3, 2, 4] ❌

2️⃣ Am I comparing two elements at a time?

    Two pointers is for problems like:

        -> pair
        -> subarray window
        -> palindrome check
        -> left vs right comparison

    Examples:

        -> Two Sum (sorted)
        -> Pair with target
        -> Reverse array
        -> Palindrome

3️⃣ Does moving pointers shrink the search space?

    You must be able to say:
        -> “If condition is too big, move right”
        -> “If condition is too small, move left”
    If pointer movement is logical and predictable, two pointers works.

4️⃣ Are indices or values allowed to be returned?

    If original indices matter and array is unsorted → ❌ two pointers
    If only values or sorted indices matter → ✅ two pointers

5️⃣ Can I do better than O(n²)?
    Two pointers is almost always:
        O(n) time
        O(1) space

🧠 Golden Rule (MEMORIZE THIS)
 -> ❝Sorted + pair-based + monotonic movement = Two Pointers❞